affineFatPoints -- produces the ideal and initial ideal from the coordinates of a finite set of fat points
**********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (Q,inG,G) = affineFatPoints(M,mults,R)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, in which each column consists
        of the coordinates of a point
      * mults, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, in which each element
        determines the multiplicity of the corresponding point
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, coordinate ring of the affine
        space containing the points
  * Outputs:
      * Q, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of standard monomials
      * inG, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, initial ideal of the set of
        fat points
      * G, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of generators for Grobner
        basis for ideal of fat points

Description
===========

This function uses a modified Buchberger-Moeller algorithm to compute a grobner
basis for the ideal of a finite number of fat points in affine space.



