randomPointsMat -- matrix of homogeneous coordinates of random points in projective space
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        m=randomPointsMat(R,n)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, homogeneous coordinate ring of
        projective space Pm
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of points
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * AllRandom => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * m, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of ZZ

Description
===========

Produces a random m+1 x n matrix of scalars, with columns representing the
coordinates of the point. The first m+1 x m+1 submatrix is the identity.

